{
  "about": "Which cheat sheets semantic retrieval searches (rule R3, design decision 28). Decided from each sheet's title and opening paragraph only, never from retrieval output. Used only when SEMANTIC_KB_SCOPE is on; map retrieval ignores this file. Every sheet in kb/docs is listed exactly once: under excluded, platform or general. The common set (common.json) is always searched.",
  "rules": {
    "retired": "a. Title starts with \"DEPRECATED:\" or contains \"(Historical)\". Excluded.",
    "attack_catalogue": "b. The sheet is mainly attack inputs rather than defensive guidance. Excluded.",
    "platform": "c. The sheet is specific to one language, framework or runtime (tagged when its title or opening names that one as its scope). Excluded unless the tag equals KB_TARGET_PLATFORM. Untagged sheets are general and kept; platform-neutral infrastructure sheets (Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD) stay untagged."
  },
